From f624958e67d5f1c5a9f3f37ba04109a1ab95641e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Etienne Carriere <etienne.carriere@foss.st.com>
Date: Mon, 8 Jul 2024 09:56:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1191/1695] core: arm: pageable PM sequences

Allow Arm PM sequence for 32bit machines to be almost fully pageable,
relaxing the pressure on the secure internal RAM, more specifically on
the physical pages pool of the pager. The feature is under configuration
switches CFG_PAGED_PSCI_SYSTEM_OFF and CFG_PAGED_PSCI_SYSTEM_SUSPEND.

The PSCI fastcall SMC already reach smc_std_handler() and
tee_psci_handler() functions. These 2 are modified to pass a new
argument that is the PSCI function to be called in a pageable context,
and then both return a status on whether the PSCI service was executed
(SM_EXIT_TO_NON_SECURE) or the PSCI service is to be executed in a
thread and pageable context (SM_EXIT_TO_PM_THREAD).

When a thread/pageable PSCI handler is to be called, secure monitor
exists to secure world through new vector_thread_pm_entry() with PSCI
handler function arguments in thread_smc_args::r0..r5 and handler
entry address in argument thread_smc_args::r6.
In turn vector_thread_pm_entry() calls thread_handle_pm() to allocate
the thread. Function thread_handle_pm() may return with an error
status if no thread context is available. Because the PM sequences are
expected to be uninterruptible, flag THREAD_FLAGS_NATIVE_INTR_DISABLE
is define for OP-TEE native (secure) interrupts to be masked in the
pageable PM thread context.

Generic 32bit PM helper function sm_pm_cpu_do_suspend() and
sm_pm_cpu_do_resume() are changed to save and restore the FIQ, abort
and undefined exception contexts and are declared unpaged.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git 7ab388fc23a46aa01342a6c291a21aa31a578d50 core: arm: pageable PM sequences]
